#: ../../../developer_guide/testing_style.md:1
msgid "Testing Style Guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/testing_style.md:3
msgid ""
"Bug fixes need regression coverage, not automatically another test. Add or "
"expand tests only for behavior the existing suite does not already protect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/testing_style.md:6
msgid ""
"**Identify the gap.** Name the failure and the assertion that catches it. "
"Check nearby tests and their target/pass settings; a passing suite alone is "
"not proof of coverage. Verify failure before the fix when practical."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/testing_style.md:9
msgid ""
"**Extend before duplicating.** Prefer a small case or assertion in the "
"relevant test family. Reuse kernels, verifiers, and setup instead of copying "
"a test file for a minor variant. A separate test is fine for different "
"behavior or setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/testing_style.md:12
msgid ""
"**Assert behavior, not the patch.** Do not scan repository source for the "
"fix, assert constants or mock results unrelated to the bug, or compute the "
"expected result with the implementation under test. Keep runtime coverage "
"when only execution exposes the failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/testing_style.md:16
msgid ""
"**Keep cases focused.** Use the smallest input that still triggers the bug. "
"Add shapes, dtypes, and configurations only for distinct affected paths, "
"boundaries, or necessary interactions. Avoid unrelated parameter products "
"and repeated kernel compilation that add cost without coverage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/testing_style.md:20
msgid ""
"**Keep the change local.** Reuse existing helpers; do not introduce a "
"fixture framework or refactor unrelated tests for a small regression."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer_guide/testing_style.md:23
msgid ""
"If existing tests already catch the failure, run them rather than add an "
"equivalent permanent test. Preserve distinct regression coverage: fewer test "
"functions or files is not the goal."
msgstr ""
